chip ym2612
clock 7670453
samples 30000
# The timers, status and IRQ line. Timer A counts 0x24 (high 8 bits) and
# 0x25 (low 2) against 1024, one sample a step; timer B counts 0x26 against
# 256 in steps of 16. 0x27 loads them (bits 0 and 1), lets them set their
# status flags (bits 2 and 3) and resets the flags (bits 4 and 5). Status
# reads at offset 0 land around expiries and straight after a write, which
# shows the busy bit; offsets 1 to 3 read 0. The prescaler writes 0x2D to
# 0x2F that the YM2203 and YM2608 take do nothing on the YM2612: its rate
# stays clock / 144.
0 w 0 30 1 01 0 40 1 7f 0 50 1 1f 0 60 1 00 0 70 1 00 0 80 1 0f 0 90 1 00 0 38 1 01 0 48 1 7f 0 58 1 1f 0 68 1 00 0 78 1 00 0 88 1 0f 0 98 1 00 0 34 1 01 0 44 1 7f 0 54 1 1f 0 64 1 00 0 74 1 00 0 84 1 0f 0 94 1 00 0 3c 1 01 0 4c 1 08 0 5c 1 1f 0 6c 1 00 0 7c 1 00 0 8c 1 0f 0 9c 1 00 0 b0 1 07 0 b4 1 c0 0 a4 1 22 0 a0 1 69 0 28 1 80
